== a festival weekend
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult
age: 16-30
calls: RG
tone: joy
life: leisure, music
horizon: week
roles: friend, strangers, stewards
earth: three days of music in a muddy field, with a tent and a wristband
times: About 1 in 4 young adults, one or a few summers (estimate)
gap: .8-1
share: .25
rate: 1
# rate lowered (drafts/repeats/everyday.py)
scene: Three days in a field, forty bands, one leaking tent, and {friend} has the only working torch.
scene W: {N} has a printed schedule, a first-aid kit and the group's meeting point, and means to bring everyone home.
scene U: {N} has studied the line-up and found the one tiny stage where the interesting things happen.
scene B: The wristband says general admission. {N} has a plan for the backstage area.
scene R: The bass hits {N} in the chest, the crowd sways, and the weekend has begun.
scene G: Rain on canvas, wood smoke, and ten thousand people singing the same chorus under the open sky.
- W | stick to the group plan and check in at the meeting point every evening | v: security, conformity | chance: 90
- U | track down the obscure band on the smallest stage | v: self-direction, stimulation | chance: 92
- B | make friends with a roadie and talk your way backstage | v: power, stimulation | chance: 20
- R | dance at the front until your legs give out | v: hedonism, stimulation | body: light | chance: 95
- G | light a fire in the woods past the fence and sleep out under the stars | v: hedonism, universalism (nature) | closed: law: open fires banned; backfire: a fine, and thrown out | chance: 72
- W>B | work as a steward, and use the staff pass to wave your friends in free | v: power (resources) | closed: approval: abusing a staff pass; backfire: the pass taken, and a ban | chance: 70
- U>R | read up on the pills going round, test one, and take it | v: stimulation, hedonism | body: heavy | closed: law: illegal drugs; backfire: a bad night in the medical tent, or an arrest | law: drugs | chance: 78
- B>G | collect the tents people abandon and take them to a shelter | v: universalism, benevolence | chance: 72
- R>W | push through the crowd to help someone who has collapsed | v: benevolence | body: light | mark: helped someone in need | chance: 90
- G>U | wander into the drumming circle and learn the rhythms by ear | door | v: self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 78
works: {N} comes home sunburnt, hoarse and happy, with three new friends.
works: The best set of the weekend is one nobody else saw, and {N} was there for it.
fails: The tent floods on the first night, and the weekend turns into a test of survival.
fails: {N} loses the group, the phone and the wristband, in that order.

== your first tax form and a stack of bills
tier: everyday
at: ministry
stages: young_adult
age: 17-30
calls: WUB
tone: trouble
life: money
horizon: week
roles: parent, friend, the tax office
earth: a brown envelope from the tax office, and four bills underneath it
times: Nearly every young adult, once, with the first job or the first flat (estimate)
once: yes
scene: The envelope from the tax office sits on top of the pile, unopened, and the pile is growing.
scene W: {N} wants it done properly: every form filled in, every bill paid, nothing owed to anyone.
scene U: Somewhere in all this paperwork there is a system, and {N} wants to understand it.
scene B: There are allowances, deductions and loopholes in here, and {N} suspects most people leave money on the table.
scene R: The forms are boring beyond words, and {N} would rather do anything else at all.
scene G: {parent} always kept the family's papers in a shoebox under the bed and did them once a year, at the kitchen table.
- W | fill in every form honestly and pay each bill the day it arrives | habit | v: conformity, security | chance: 90
- U | learn how the system works and build a budget that tracks everything | v: security, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | chance: 82
- B | claim expenses you never had, and pay a little less | v: power (resources) | mark: hid a wrong | closed: law: tax fraud; backfire: an audit, a fine and the back tax | chance: 82
- R | put music on, pour a drink, and tear through the whole pile in one night | v: security, hedonism | chance: 70
- G | take the pile home and do it with your parents at the kitchen table | v: tradition, security | chance: 85
- W>G | pay the bills first, then send something home every month, without fail | binds | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 75
- U>W | read the small print, find the overcharge, and claim it back | v: security, universalism (fairness) | chance: 45
- B>U | trade favours with an accountant friend to learn the tricks | v: self-direction, power | chance: 72
- R>B | ring the energy company, and charm your way to a better deal | v: power | chance: 55
- G>R | decide it will all work out somehow, and book a weekend away | v: hedonism | chance: 12
works: The forms go in, the bills are paid, and there is even a small refund.
works: {N} sits back from the kitchen table with every paper sorted, feeling like a grown-up.
fails: A final demand arrives, with a late fee attached.
fails: The tax office writes back: there is a mistake, and it is {Ns}.

