== your parents expect you home for the holidays
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult
age: 17-30
calls: WG
tone: mixed
life: family, tradition
horizon: week
roles: parent, grandparent, sibling, friend
earth: the family expects everyone home for the winter holidays, as always
times: Most young adults with parents alive, every year at the winter holidays (estimate)
gap: .8-1
scene: {parent} has already asked twice: will {N} be home for the holidays, like every year?
scene W: The family has always gathered on the same day, at the same table, and an empty chair would be noticed.
scene U: {N} weighs it up: the cost of the train, the week of work lost, the arguments sure to come, the people {N} misses.
scene B: Going home means a free week of food and comfort, and maybe a quiet word with the uncle who owns the business.
scene R: {friend} has a cabin in the mountains for the same week, and the invitation is burning a hole in {Ns} phone.
scene G: The house will smell of the same spices it always does, and {grandparent} is a year older every winter.
- W | go home as always, and play your part in every ritual | habit | v: tradition, conformity | chance: 80
- U | go for exactly three days, planned so nobody can argue | v: self-direction, security | chance: 75
- B | go, and use the week to talk the rich uncle into backing your plans | v: power, achievement | chance: 30
- R | tell them you are going to the mountains with friends instead | identity | v: self-direction, stimulation | mark: defied an authority | chance: 70
- G | go home early to cook with your grandmother, while she still can | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 87
- W>R | go home out of duty, then slip out to the old pub with school friends | v: hedonism, conformity | chance: 82
- U>G | record your grandparents telling the old family stories | v: tradition | chance: 90
- B>W | skip the trip, but send gifts expensive enough that nobody can complain | v: conformity, power (face) | chance: 45
- R>U | ask at the dinner table the family questions nobody dares to ask | v: self-direction | chance: 45
- G>B | stay a month instead of a week, living off the family again | v: security, hedonism | chance: 50
works: The holiday is warm and loud, and {N} leaves with a bag full of leftovers.
works: For once there is no argument at the table, and {grandparent} laughs all evening.
fails: The old argument with {parent} flares on the first night and never quite dies down.
fails: {N} spends the week feeling like a sulking teenager again.

