# ---------------------------------------------------------------- pair 6: calls WB (cycle s4) / calls URG (cycle s2)

== a job interview
tier: everyday
at: employer
stages: young_adult
age: 17-30
calls: WB
tone: mixed
life: work
horizon: moment
roles: boss, parent, friend, an interview panel
earth: an interview for a job you want, at nine on Monday
times: Most young adults, about once a year while starting out; Americans hold about 12 jobs from 18 to their mid-fifties, nearly half before 25 (BLS)
gap: .8-1
scene: Monday, nine o'clock: a glass office and a panel of three. {N} has a new shirt and a dry mouth.
scene W: {N} arrives fifteen minutes early, with copies of everything, ready to show they can be relied on.
scene U: {N} has researched the firm, the panel, and the questions this kind of panel always asks.
scene B: The job pays well and leads somewhere. {N} wants it, and knows everyone else in the waiting room wants it too.
scene R: {Ns} heart hammers. Ten minutes in a room, and the next five years hang on it.
scene G: {N} is not sure this place is right, and keeps noticing how tired the people in the corridor look.
- W | answer every question honestly, even the ones that show your weak spots | identity | v: benevolence (honesty), conformity | mark: owned up | chance: 48
- U | rehearse answers to every likely question until they are flawless | v: achievement | chance: 60
- B | bring proof of everything you have done, and sell it hard | v: achievement, power | chance: 60
- R | throw away the script and just be yourself, loudly | v: self-direction | chance: 50
- G | ask what the work is really like, and watch the faces in the corridor | v: security, self-direction | chance: 42
- W>G | ask, politely and plainly, whether the hours leave room for family | v: benevolence, security | chance: 40
- U>W | bring a short written plan for improving their service | v: achievement, conformity | chance: 55
- B>U | flatter the interviewer into talking, and learn what they really want | v: power | chance: 65
- R>B | name your salary straight out, and do not blink | v: power, achievement | chance: 55
- G>R | decide halfway through that this is not your life, and walk out | identity | v: self-direction | mark: turned down a chance | chance: 75
works: The phone rings the next afternoon: the job is {Ns} if {N} wants it.
works: The interview turns into a long, easy conversation, and {N} walks out already knowing.
fails: The letter says, politely, that they have chosen someone else.
fails: {N} freezes on the second question and never quite recovers.

== awake at night worrying about the future
