scene U: {N} has drawn a floor plan, priced the furniture and worked out what living together will cost, to the penny.
scene B: Two salaries, one rent. {N} sees the sums, and the space, and the bigger flat they can now afford.
scene R: {N} carries {partner} over the threshold, laughing, and they collapse onto a mattress on the floor.
scene G: {N} puts {grandparent}'s old plant on the windowsill, and the place starts to feel like a home.
- W | sit down together and agree house rules, chores and money, in writing | v: conformity, security | chance: 72
- U | plan the move like a project: lists, budgets and a timetable | v: security, achievement | chance: 70
