horizon: months
roles: partner, friend, parent, sibling
earth: the relationship ends: a long talk, a closed door, a box of things to give back
scene: It is over between {N} and {partner}. One of them said it out loud at last, and the other did not argue.
scene W: {N} made promises to {partner}, and now they lie broken on the kitchen table beside the spare keys.
scene U: {N} keeps replaying the last year, looking for the exact moment it started to go wrong.
scene B: {N} counts what is left: the flat, the friends, the furniture, and who will keep what.
scene R: {Ns} heart is in pieces, and {N} wants to scream, to cry, to smash every plate in the cupboard.
scene G: Some things grow and some things die back. {N} knows this, and tonight it does not help at all.
- W | divide things fairly, keep it civil, and keep what promises you still can | v: universalism (fairness), conformity | mark: kept your word | chance: 65
- U | write it all out until you understand what went wrong | habit | v: self-direction | chance: 70
- B | make sure you keep the friends and everything worth having, and let them start again | v: power (resources), security | chance: 70
- R | go dancing with your friends that night, and cry on their shoulders after | v: hedonism, benevolence | chance: 80
- G | stay close to your family for a while, and let it heal | v: security, tradition | chance: 80
- BR | go out every night and make sure your ex sees the photos | habit | v: hedonism, power (face) | chance: 55
- UG | take long walks and slowly work out what you need next time | door | v: self-direction | chance: 80
- UR | pour it all into a song or a story that is brutally honest | habit | identity | v: self-direction | chance: 78
- WB | insist on getting back everything you lent and every penny you are owed | v: security, power (resources) | chance: 65
- WG | stay kind to them, and stay friends for the sake of your shared circle | v: benevolence, tradition | chance: 55
works: The friends rally round, and {N} comes out of it surer of what they want.
works: Months later {N} can think of {partner} without it hurting, and that feels like freedom.
fails: The breakup drags on for months, bitter and public.
fails: {N} spends a long, dark winter barely leaving the flat.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: your first full-time job (triads from D4a)
# Every option is a way of starting the job, so every option carries commit:career (each color twice in all).

== your first full-time job
tier: life event
at: employer
stages: young_adult adult
age: 16-35
per_year: 0 0 .2 .3 0 0
drivers: prosper+.5 ties+.3 money+.2 health+.2 unrest-.4 fortune+.1
excludes: career
domain: career1
rite: adult
once: yes
times: once; most people start a first full-time job between eighteen and twenty-five, later after long study: about 20 in 100 young adults and 30 in 100 adults still without one start it each year (D13 counts any new job, so this is an estimate scaled down to first jobs); a teenager's first part-time job is your first real job
likelier: a growing economy, a finished degree or apprenticeship, family contacts and friends who hear of openings, a move to a city, good health
rarer: a recession, war or unrest, poor health or a disability without support, no money to live on while searching, long study
tone: mixed
life: work
horizon: years
roles: boss, colleague, mentor, parent
earth: a contract, a desk or a station of your own, and a first full month's pay
scene: Monday morning: {N} has a lanyard with their name on it, a contract in a drawer, and no idea where anything is.
scene W: {N} has signed a contract and means to keep every line of it: on time, every day, doing the job right.
scene U: Everything is new: the systems, the jargon, the unwritten rules. {N} is taking notes on all of it.
scene B: {N} looks at the chart of names on the wall and counts the steps from the bottom to the top.
scene R: The first pay arrives in four weeks, and {N} already knows exactly how to spend it.
scene G: {N} has found work that suits their hands and their pace, and the old hands on the team have taken them in.
- W | turn up early every day and learn to do the job exactly right | v: conformity, achievement | tags: commit:career | chance: 80
- U | learn every system in the place until you understand it better than anyone | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: learned a skill | tags: commit:career | chance: 72
- B | set your sights on your boss's job from the first week | identity | v: power, achievement | tags: commit:career | chance: 68
- R | throw yourself in, say yes to everything, and spend the first pay on a party | door | v: hedonism, stimulation | tags: commit:career | chance: 90
- G | settle in among the old hands and learn the work at their pace | v: tradition, security | tags: commit:career | chance: 80
- WUR | find a demanding mentor and train hard, mind and nerve, to master the craft | binds | v: achievement, self-direction | tags: commit:career | chance: 70
- WUB | climb by the book: exams, certificates and the right introductions | v: achievement, power | tags: commit:career | chance: 65
- WBG | stay in it for years, steady, saving every month toward a home | habit | v: security, tradition | tags: commit:career | chance: 72
- URG | teach yourself the job your own way, trusting your instincts over the manual | v: self-direction | tags: commit:career | closed: approval: ignoring the firm's procedures; backfire: a formal warning | chance: 62
- BRG | fight your way up from the bottom, louder and hungrier than the rest | v: achievement, power | tags: commit:career | chance: 68
works: By the end of the first month {N} knows everyone's name, and the job feels like theirs.
works: {boss} stops by at the end of the quarter to say the team is glad to have {N}.
fails: The work is grinding, the hours are long, and {N} dreads every Sunday evening.
fails: {N} makes a serious mistake in the second week and spends months living it down.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: losing your job (triads from D4b)

== losing your job
tier: life event
at: employer
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 17-75
per_year: 0 0 .08 .05 .04 .02
drivers: prosper-.6 unrest+.5 era+.4 ties-.2 trouble+.15
gap: 1-3
needs: career
domain: career1
rite: adult mature
times: zero to three times in a working life: per worker about 8 in 100 young adults, 5 in 100 adults, 4 in 100 in midlife and 2 in 100 older workers a year lose a job through a layoff, a closure or a job cut, about twice that in a recession (D57, data and estimate)
likelier: a recession, unrest, a young firm or a shrinking trade, a closing factory, short contracts, new technology in the trade, little schooling
rarer: a growing economy, education and rare skills, public-sector or union work, long service, contacts who can find you work
ends: career
tone: trouble
life: work, money
horizon: months
roles: boss, colleague, parent, partner, friend
earth: a meeting with the manager and someone from personnel, a box for your things, and two weeks' notice
scene: Friday, four o'clock: a meeting with {boss} and someone from personnel, a cardboard box, and two weeks' pay.
scene W: {N} did everything that was asked, and it made no difference. The rules, it turns out, were never the whole story.
scene U: {N} walks out into the street already working out what went wrong: the firm, the market, and their own part in it.
scene B: The firm protected the people at the top, as firms do. {N} notes it, and notes who kept their jobs.
scene R: {N} shakes with anger on the bus home, swearing under their breath at every stop.
scene G: The whole trade is shrinking, like a river in a dry year. {N} saw it coming and hoped it would not reach them.
- W | sign on for benefits straight away and apply for jobs every single day | v: security, conformity | chance: 54
- U | take stock of your skills and retrain for a field that is growing | binds | v: self-direction, achievement | mark: learned a skill | chance: 53
- B | set up on your own the next week, and win clients fair and square | identity | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 40
- R | tell your boss exactly what you think of them on the way out | v: self-direction | mark: made an enemy | chance: 48
- G | move in with family, and work cash in hand for people you know | binds | v: tradition, security | closed: law: undeclared work; backfire: a fine, and benefits stopped | chance: 56
- WUG | take the time to work out, calmly, what work you were really meant for | door | v: self-direction, security | chance: 55
- WRG | rally the others let go and occupy the office until the firm pays | v: universalism (fairness), benevolence | closed: law: occupying the premises; backfire: removed by the police, and blacklisted | chance: 38
- WBR | take the first decent offer within a week and get moving | v: achievement, security | chance: 60
- UBR | forge a glowing reference and talk your way into a better job | v: achievement, power | mark: hid a wrong | closed: law: forgery; backfire: found out at the reference check, and the offer withdrawn | chance: 58
- UBG | live on next to nothing, sell what you can, and wait for the right opening | v: security, power (resources) | chance: 42
works: Within two months {N} has a new job, and a better one.
works: Six months later {N} is doing work they had never thought of, and likes it.
fails: The savings run out before the job offers start.
fails: {N} sends out a hundred applications and gets three replies.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: a baby on the way, planned or not (cross cycle s3; pairs D5a)
# The five one-color options and the s3 cycle meet the coming child: each carries commit:children and binds (even per
# color). R14 (Emren, release checklist section 10): ending the pregnancy and planning an adoption are pickable, in plain
# words, for a character of either sex (the pregnancy may be the partner's, and the choice is then made together). The
# pair set D5a holds them: BG, UB, UR and WR end the pregnancy, each in its own way (law: abortion), and WG sees it
# through and plans for another family to adopt the baby (law: adoption). None of the five carries commit:children or
# binds, so the person can meet this moment again later. None is written closed: the modern law book (chroma-engine
# world.py LAW_MOD) has both legal, so with the world off they stay open; with it on, the law book opens, restricts or
# bans them. Backfire wording for a banned state, for the game: ending it, "found out, and charged, with the clinic
# closed down"; adoption, "the papers refused, and the baby placed by the court instead".
# Rates: in rich countries about 1 in 5 known pregnancies end in abortion (US about 1 in 5, Guttmacher Institute; England
# and Wales about 1 in 4 conceptions, ONS), more among the young, the childless and the unplanned (about 4 in 10
# unintended US pregnancies, Finer and Zolna 2016); placing a newborn for adoption is rare, well under 1 in 100 births
# (US about 18,000 a year against 3.6 million births, National Council for Adoption). The engine picks a pair option
# about half as often as a one-color one, so ending it takes four pairs at high felt odds (chance 88 to 90) and the
# adoption one pair at low ones (chance 20).
# Measured in the engine (a copy of engtest20, 600 lives, seeds 51-54): of 437 pregnancies met, 19 in 100 end
# (20 of the first ones), 3 in 100 go to adoption (above the real share, but one option of fifteen at low felt odds
# goes little lower) and 78 are kept.

== a baby on the way, planned or not
tier: life event
at: hospital
stages: young_adult
age: 16-32
per_year: 0 0 .12 0 0 0
drivers: family+.4 community+.3 prosper+.2 money+.1 stress-.3 unrest-.2
excludes: children
domain: children1
rite: adult
times: zero to two first pregnancies in this stage: per young adult with no children yet about 12 in 100 a year (D04, data: 55.8 births per 1,000 women at 20-24, 12.6 at 15-19, set per eligible person by the engine at pull-in, 06:29), and about four in ten pregnancies at this age are unplanned; later births come through a child is born
likelier: a settled partner or marriage, a faith or family that hopes for children, family nearby, rural life, a growing economy, less schooling
rarer: long study, a demanding first career, money worries, stress, unsettled times, poor health, no partner
tone: mixed
life: children, family
horizon: years
roles: parent, sibling, friend, partner, a midwife
earth: a positive test, two lines on a little stick
scene: There it is: two lines on a little plastic stick, and {N} sitting on the edge of the bath, staring at them.
scene W: {N} feels the weight of it at once: a life to be responsible for, and every promise that comes with it.
scene U: {N} is already reading: weeks, stages, costs, leave rules. There is so much to learn before the spring.
scene B: {N} thinks of the job, the flat, the money and the plans, and what each of them will cost now.
scene R: {Ns} heart leaps and lurches at the same time: terror, joy and disbelief, all at once.
scene G: {N} feels it like the turn of a season: something has begun that is older than any plan.
- W | tell the family at once, and do right by everyone from day one | identity | binds | v: conformity, tradition | mark: owned up | tags: commit:children | chance: 85
- U | read every book and plan the next year month by month | binds | v: security, self-direction | tags: commit:children | chance: 90
- B | keep your own plans first, and line up all the help you can from the start | identity | binds | v: achievement, power | tags: commit:children | act: keep their own plans first, and line up all the help they can from the start | chance: 75
- R | shout the news from the rooftops, and work out the rest later | binds | v: stimulation | tags: commit:children | chance: 78
- G | trust nature and your family, and let the months unfold | binds | v: tradition, security | tags: commit:children | chance: 78
- W>R | promise yourself the baby will join your adventures, not end them | binds | v: hedonism, stimulation | tags: commit:children | chance: 60
- U>G | research gentle, natural birth and plan one with care | binds | v: universalism (nature), security | tags: commit:children | chance: 68
- B>W | chase every grant, benefit and family offer, and put it all toward a safe home | binds | v: security, power (resources) | tags: commit:children | chance: 80
- R>U | panic, then sign up for every class going and ask a hundred questions | binds | v: self-direction, security | tags: commit:children | chance: 90
- G>B | lean on your family's help, so your own plans need not stop | binds | v: achievement, tradition | tags: commit:children | chance: 70
- BG | tell only your closest family, and end the pregnancy quietly | v: security, tradition | law: abortion | chance: 90
- UB | count what a child would cost right now, and end the pregnancy early | v: security, achievement | law: abortion | chance: 90
- UR | get the facts from a doctor, then follow your heart and end the pregnancy | v: self-direction | law: abortion | chance: 88
- WG | see the pregnancy through, and choose a loving family to adopt the baby | v: benevolence, security | law: adoption | chance: 20
- WR | end the pregnancy, and say so openly to anyone who asks | v: self-direction, universalism | law: abortion | chance: 88
works: The choice, once made, feels like {Ns} own, and the months after it go more gently than {N} feared.
works: {parent} hears it all over a long evening at the kitchen table, and stands by {N} whatever comes next.
fails: The weeks of deciding are hard: sleepless nights, money fears and arguments about everything.
fails: The news splits the family, and {N} faces most of it alone.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: an unexpected chance (the four-color set)
# The five four-color options take the chance as a calling: each carries commit:career (each color once in all).

== an unexpected chance: a grant, a role, a stage
tier: life event
stages: young_adult adult
age: 17-60
per_year: 0 0 .04 .04 0 0
drivers: prosper+.3 ties+.3 community+.3 money+.2 unrest-.3 fortune+.15
gap: 3-8
domain: career.5
rite: adult
times: zero to three in a life: about 4 in 100 young adults and adults a year are picked or honoured for their work: a funded place, a part, a first big stage (D22, estimate)
likelier: years of work behind it, a mentor or a network, a community that knows the work, money to make it seen, a city, a growing economy
rarer: isolation, no contacts, low money, a recession, unrest, discrimination, a closed field
tone: joy
life: work, calling
horizon: years
roles: mentor, boss, parent, partner, friend
earth: a letter offering a funded place, a lead role, or a first big stage
scene: The letter is short: {N} has been chosen. A funded year, a role, a stage, the thing {N} has wanted for years, starting next month.
scene W: {N} has been chosen above many others, and feels the weight of living up to that trust.
scene U: It is a chance to go deeper than ever before: a year to learn, to test, to do the work properly.
scene B: Doors that were shut yesterday are open today. {N} sees exactly how far this could go.
scene R: {N} reads the letter four times, then screams into a pillow.
scene G: {N} has been growing toward this for years without quite knowing it, like a tree toward a gap in the canopy.
- W | accept, and work every day to deserve the honour | v: conformity, achievement | chance: 76
- U | accept, and spend the first month studying everything the role demands | v: self-direction, achievement | chance: 78
- B | use the offer to bargain for something better elsewhere | door | v: power, achievement | chance: 70
- R | say yes on the spot, without reading the terms | v: stimulation | mark: took a wild risk | chance: 75
- G | turn it down; the timing is wrong, and the family needs a hand at home | identity | v: tradition, benevolence | mark: turned down a chance | chance: 60
- WUBG | accept, and build on it slowly for years, with a plan and a home base | binds | v: achievement, security | tags: commit:career | chance: 78
- WUBR | take it, move to the city, and remake yourself to fit the part | v: achievement, self-direction | mark: moved away | tags: commit:career | chance: 65
- WURG | accept, and share every door it opens with friends and family | v: benevolence, universalism | tags: commit:career | chance: 72
- WBRG | take it and fight to the top of the field before the chance can close | v: achievement, power | tags: commit:career | chance: 65
- UBRG | take it, break every rule of the field, and make it your own | identity | v: self-direction, stimulation | tags: commit:career | chance: 45
works: The year that follows is the best of {Ns} life so far.
works: {N} makes the most of it, and people in the field start to know the name.
fails: The chance turns out to be smaller than it looked, and much harder.
fails: {N} freezes under the weight of it, and the moment slips away.
